  message: "Astro repro (from WI-pifus, 2026-10-01; corpus nuclear, survey --include-docs on branch jgstern-agent/fix/pifus @ f13f35fb0f, which fixes astro's root-relative paths; output in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/pifus/nuclear-after.json). The mechanism named here holds for astro, at TWO sites, not only the astro.py:314 site cited above:\n(a) frontmatter import edge, astro.py `_parse_frontmatter_js`: dst = f\"astro:{import_path}:1-1:file:file\" built from the RAW import string, e.g. index.astro -> astro:../components/Hero.astro:1-1:file:file. This id has 5 slots, so WI-bufar's slot-count gate does not flag it, but its path slot is the unresolved relative string; the materialized node's path '../components/Hero.astro' does not exist under the root.\n(b) component-reference edge, astro.py `_process_tag` (the :314 site): dst = import_path bare, e.g. index.astro -> ../components/Hero.astro:<unknown>:0-0:../components/Hero.astro:external_symbol.\nCount on nuclear: 21 astro imports edges; 18 name an existing in-repo .astro file (resolved against the importer's directory: packages/website/src/components/{Badge,Box,Downloads,Hero,Screenshots}.astro, packages/website/src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro); 0 of those 18 land on that file's node (9 via site a, 9 via site b). The other 3 are unimported components (Element, Icon, Image) with the astro:component:<Name> placeholder. Also observed, not investigated: Hero.astro has no astro file node at all in the survey (it mints no symbols or edge srcs; astro sets create_file_symbols=False), so a resolver pointing at make_file_id(\"astro\", target) would land on an id with no node for such files. Before WI-pifus the importer side was also wrong (src path carried the root directory's name), so resolving against the importer's directory was impossible until that fix."  # 5a7c
